30,2,1,talk,Midori,,It seems we have a history of joint ventures failing due to rota disputes and external visits being unreliable. We should be cautious about programs relying on other departments or home visits.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I found that a previous call-back trial significantly reduced readmissions for the elderly, though the effect vanished when it ended. It proves that follow-up care works if it's consistent.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The staffing situation is precarious. Ward nursing is struggling with vacancies and agency costs, but interestingly, the midwifery rota has quite a bit of slack due to lower birth numbers.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The budget is tighter than usual, and floor space costs now eat into it. Furthermore, we only earn revenue for on-site sessions. Home-based care is a financial liability.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Shizue,,I'm afraid our physical capacity is nearly at its limit. The parking fills up early and the shuttle is limited. Any program requiring more on-site visits might cause a bottleneck.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, if home visits are a financial drain and @Misaki says ward nurses are stretched, perhaps we should avoid the Home Follow-Up Team.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, while I see the risk, the readmission data shows a real need for that kind of care. However, we must ensure it's recorded properly, as the booking system is limited.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"If we want something that won't burn out the staff, the Perinatal Support Service seems viable since midwifery has the capacity.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, that is a logical point. On-site services are the only ones that generate tariffs, which helps offset the reduced development budget.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with @Misaki. If we use existing slack in the midwifery rota, we might avoid adding too much pressure to the already crowded outpatient rooms.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, would the Perinatal service require too much parking or shuttle use? If it's targeted, it might be manageable.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,It seems the Day Rehabilitation Unit would put the most pressure on the parking and rooms @Shizue mentioned.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Misaki,,And the therapy staffing review shows we are losing physiotherapists. A Day Rehab Unit might be impossible to staff.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Exactly. The Day Rehab Unit requires floor space, which is now expensive, and staff we don't have. It is an inefficient choice.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I feel the same. The Perinatal service seems the most gentle fit for our current situation.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Midori,,I'm leaning toward the Perinatal Support Service too. It avoids the pitfalls of the joint-clinic failures if the midwifery lead is clear.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I still value the impact of follow-ups, but given the staffing and budget constraints, the Perinatal service is the most realistic.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I'm satisfied with that. It supports the staff and the patients without overloading the ward nurses.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Shion,,It is the only option that aligns with the financial reality and the available human resources.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I am happy we have found a path that keeps the hospital running smoothly for everyone.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
